d out; finished in 0.22s\ntest result: ok. 6 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.10s\n-- symbol diff (C vs Rust) under default / --no-default-features --\nsymbol diff: EMPTY (parity)\nALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4apbom6pu6hrjgb7vwrlge5rrgoswpkbanyilvj66es7ztap6ztq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte. No divergences found; no changes to `src/lib.rs` were needed.**\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- [x] **`SYMBOLS.md`** — symbol diff is empty. Both `.so`s export exactly `driver`; the C `static`s (`multi_stage`, `y`) correctly stay unexported. 0 unresolved non-libc symbols (`ldd -r` clean + live `dlopen`).\n- [x] **Phase B** — all 20 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass (22 tests), incl. the exhaustive 12³ boundary cross-product and seeded randomized sweeps.\n- [x] **Binary stdout** — N/A: no `add_executable` / no `[[bin]]`. Asserted as a guard test so the claim can't rot.\n- [x] **Phase C** — all 10 `ERRORS.md` rows pass (11 tests), each asserting the exact rejection bytes *and* the numeric `result` sentinel for both libraries.\n- [x] **All feature combinations** — `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` and the C has no `#ifdef`, so the default build is the whole matrix; enforced by a test and by the power-set loop in `scripts/run_tests.sh`.\n\n**Total: 39/39 tests passing.**\n\n## Artifacts written\n\n| file | contents |\n|---|---|\n| `translation/SYMBOLS.md` | symbol surface + parity diff + mutation-test results |\n| `translation/ERRORS.md` | 10-row error table (3 `goto fail` branches, epilogue, check-order, int extremes, bit patterns, state) |\n| `translation/CONFIGS.md` | 20-row config table (A1–A8 branch axes) |\n| `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` | `libloading` harness — loads *both* `.so`s, calls only exported `driver`, captures fd 1 |\n| `translation/tests/phase_{b,c,d}_*.rs` | the three phases |\n| `translation/scripts/run_tests.sh` | builds C + Rust, loops feature power set, diffs symbols |\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **`RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` is required.** The library's only output is libc `stdout`, so the harness must redirect the process-global fd 1. My first run showed five \"divergences\" that were purely libtest's own progress lines leaking into the capture file. Fixed by flushing *both* buffering layers (Rust's `Stdout` LineWriter, which holds the newline-less `test foo ... ` fragment, and libc's `stdout` FILE) and enforcing serial execution with an explicit error message. `scripts/run_tests.sh` sets it.\n\n2. **Negative control.** Since a passing suite proves nothing on its own, I injected 9 mutations into `src/lib.rs` one at a time. 8/8 behaviour-changing ones were caught (off-by-one, swapped check order, dropped epilogue, wrong result code, message typo, dropped newline, stale global). The 9th — changing `AtomicI32::new(123)` to `new(0)` — was correctly *not* caught: `driver` writes the static before any read, so the C's `= 123` initialiser is provably dead. `src/lib.rs` was restored and verified byte-identical.\n\nAlso note `cargo` needed `--offline` (crates.io is proxy-blocked here); `libloading 0.8.9` was already in the local registry cache. `c_src/` is unmodified apart from the untracked `build/` directory."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":633,"cache_read_input_tokens":99006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":633,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6088e3be-5b6e-4863-a12c-1e9428a7838b","uuid":"032c6833-0125-456e-967f-990b380fc049","timestamp":"2026-09-05T04:21:44.825Z"}
